        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.103,
            0.893,
            0.137
          ],
          "content": "**8. In the electrolytic refining of a metal M, what would you take as the anode, the cathode and the electrolyte?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.14,
            0.892,
            0.173
          ],
          "content": "**9. Pratyush took sulphur powder on a spatula and heated it. He collected the gas evolved by inverting a test tube over it, as shown in figure below.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.181,
            0.176,
            0.521,
            0.193
          ],
          "content": "**(a) What will be the action of gas on**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.233,
            0.192,
            0.438,
            0.209
          ],
          "content": "**(i) dry litmus paper?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.229,
            0.208,
            0.454,
            0.225
          ],
          "content": "**(ii) moist litmus paper?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.181,
            0.224,
            0.495,
            0.273
          ],
          "content": "**(b) Write a balanced chemical equation for the reaction taking place.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.142,
            0.276,
            0.494,
            0.309
          ],
          "content": "**10. State two ways to prevent the rusting of iron.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.141,
            0.311,
            0.494,
            0.345
          ],
          "content": "**11. What type of oxides are formed when non-metals combine with oxygen?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.142,
            0.348,
            0.302,
            0.363
          ],
          "content": "**12. Give reasons**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.181,
            0.364,
            0.494,
            0.396
          ],
          "content": "**(a) Platinum, gold and silver are used to make jewellery.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.18,
            0.396,
            0.494,
            0.428
          ],
          "content": "**(b) Sodium, potassium and lithium are stored under oil.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.182,
            0.428,
            0.495,
            0.476
          ],
          "content": "**(c) Aluminium is a highly reactive metal, yet it is used to make utensils for cooking.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.181,
            0.477,
            0.496,
            0.541
          ],
          "content": "**(d) Carbonate and sulphide ores are usually converted into oxides during the process of extraction.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.501,
            0.201,
            0.882,
            0.506
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_20_image_13.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.141,
            0.545,
            0.893,
            0.581
          ],
          "content": "**13. You must have seen tarnished copper vessels being cleaned with lemon or tamarind juice. Explain why these sour substances are effective in cleaning the vessels.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.141,
            0.583,
            0.892,
            0.602
          ],
          "content": "**14. Differentiate between metal and non-metal on the basis of their chemical properties.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.141,
            0.605,
            0.894,
            0.71
          ],
          "content": "**15. A man went door to door posing as a goldsmith. He promised to bring back the glitter of old and dull gold ornaments. An unsuspecting lady gave a set of gold bangles to him which he dipped in a particular solution. The bangles sparkled like new but their weight was reduced drastically. The lady was upset but after a futile argument the man beat a hasty retreat. Can you play the detective to find out the nature of the solution he had used?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.141,
            0.713,
            0.892,
            0.749
          ],
          "content": "**16. Give reasons why copper is used to make hot water tanks and not steel (an alloy of iron).**"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.101,
            0.916,
            0.269,
            0.93
          ],
          "content": "Metals and Non-metals"
        },
